// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/gen-units-typegraph.py --gopp %gopp --out %t --seeds 8 | FileCheck %s
// P03.25 (GEN-14, UNI-2, R15 to R20): the range of the unit types of the
// instances of generic types on random graphs of declarations (cycles of 1
// to k declarations, mutual recursion, permuted and growing parameters,
// methods that return nested instances, generic aliases), against a
// brute-force expansion of every instance main reaches; the same text with 1
// and 8 body threads. The summaries of the declarations are made one strongly
// connected set at a time (Checker::unitRangeSum), so every input ends.
// More seeds and the timing: units-generic-typegraph*.long; through export
// data: Serialize.UnitRangeOfImportedInstances.
// CHECK: typegraph: 8 programs, {{[0-9]+}} rejected ({{[0-9]+}} instantiation cycles, {{[0-9]+}} out of range), 0 mismatches
